qq-wechat-cli 0.1.0

Local migration baselines:
  qq-cli-local 0.3.2, including the current working-tree fixes
  https://github.com/Chihiro521/qq-cli-local
  wechat-cli-local 0.3.1
  https://github.com/Chihiro521/wechat-cli-local

The WeChat adapter is a modified Rust port of portions of WeChat CLI Local and
its upstream WeChat CLI parsing/decryption logic. The CLI, process protocol,
page/WAL refresh, persistent index, Windows snapshot mapping and independent
QQ codec were rewritten for this combined project.

Upstream attribution retained from WeChat CLI Local:

WeChat CLI Local

This distribution contains modified code from WeChat CLI:
https://github.com/huohuoer/wechat-cli
(previously referenced as freestylefly/wechat-cli)

WeChat CLI credits wechat-decrypt for its database decryption and parsing:
https://github.com/ylytdeng/wechat-decrypt

Local changes include Windows data directory detection, packaging,
publication automation, and exclusion of local account/export data.
Distributed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.

The Windows core statically includes SQLite (public domain), zstd
(BSD-3-Clause OR GPL-2.0; the BSD alternative applies), RustCrypto libraries
(MIT OR Apache-2.0), rusqlite (MIT), and their dependencies. Their source
versions are pinned in native/Cargo.lock. No QQ client DLL or Python runtime
is included in this package.
